1
00:00:03,628 --> 00:00:06,005
Yeah, I miss you too, sweetie. Ha, ha.

2
00:00:06,172 --> 00:00:08,841
Okay, listen, I gotta go,
but I'll see you tonight.

3
00:00:09,008 --> 00:00:10,968
Bye-bye. Yeah, bye-bye.

4
00:00:11,135 --> 00:00:13,929
No, you hang up first.

5
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:16,181
Hello?

6
00:00:17,808 --> 00:00:19,976
Dude, I'm glad
you finally got a girlfriend...

7
00:00:20,144 --> 00:00:23,438
...but do you have to do lovey-dovey
in front of us who don't?

8
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:25,190
Actually, he might have to.

9
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:28,486
There's an economic concept
known as a "positional good"...

10
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:32,865
...In which an object is only valued
because it's not possessed by others.

11
00:00:33,032 --> 00:00:36,493
The term was coined in 1976
by economist Fred Hirsch...

12
00:00:36,661 --> 00:00:40,706
...to replace the more colloquial
but less precise "neener-neener."

13
00:00:40,873 --> 00:00:44,167
That's not true. My happiness
is not dependent on my best friend...

14
00:00:44,335 --> 00:00:46,545
-...being miserable and alone.
-Thank you.

15
00:00:46,712 --> 00:00:48,714
I'd be lying if I said it wasn't a perk.

16
00:00:50,007 --> 00:00:51,842
-Who's miserable and alone?
-Me.

17
00:00:52,009 --> 00:00:55,387
Oh. I used to be like that.
Then I got a girlfriend.

18
00:00:56,597 --> 00:01:00,267
In pre-1976 terms, "neener-neener."”

19
00:01:00,768 --> 00:01:03,353
What are you and Bernadette doing
for Valentine's Day?

20
00:01:03,521 --> 00:01:07,358
Yeah, I'm pulling out all the stops.
There's a 39.95 Lover's Special...

21
00:01:07,525 --> 00:01:08,901
...at P.F. Chang's.

22
00:01:10,027 --> 00:01:12,195
Yeah, egg rolls, dumplings,
bottomless wok.

23
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:16,241
Yeah, and you get your picture taken
on the big marble horse out front.

24
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:17,952
Given that Saint Valentine...

25
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:21,705
...was a third century Roman priest
who was stoned and beheaded...

26
00:01:21,872 --> 00:01:24,124
...wouldn't a more appropriate
celebration. ..

27
00:01:24,292 --> 00:01:27,795
...be taking one's steady gal
to witness a brutal murder?

28
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:31,215
I understand your point,
but given the choice...

29
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:33,550
...Jews always go with Chinese food.

30
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:38,055
If anyone's interested,
I'll be spending this Valentine's Day...

31
00:01:38,222 --> 00:01:40,265
...the same way
I spend every Valentine's.

32
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:43,811
Buying rotisserie chicken,
taking it home, standing over the sink...

33
00:01:43,978 --> 00:01:47,856
...and eating it out of the package
with my bare hands like an animal.

34
00:01:48,899 --> 00:01:51,818
Okay, so to sum up,
one giant marble horse...

35
00:01:51,986 --> 00:01:55,948
...one asinine comment,
one lonely man and his chicken...

36
00:01:56,115 --> 00:01:57,783
and let's see. Who's left?

37
00:01:57,950 --> 00:02:00,827
Oh, that's right, my plans.

38
00:02:03,956 --> 00:02:05,457
Isn't anyone gonna ask?

39
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:08,961
-You're gonna have sex with Penny.
-That's not what I was gonna tell you.

40
00:02:09,128 --> 00:02:11,672
It's okay. I don't mind hearing
about your sex life.

41
00:02:11,839 --> 00:02:13,674
It's his that bugs me.

42
00:02:15,926 --> 00:02:18,428
Guess who the university
is sending to Switzerland...

43
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:22,725
...to attend a conference and see the
CERN Super Collider on February 14th?

44
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:24,602
Professor Norton. God knows why.

45
00:02:24,769 --> 00:02:28,314
He hasn't published anything of note
since he won that Nobel Prize.

46
00:02:28,481 --> 00:02:31,484
Professor Norton can't make it.
He threw his back out climbing.

47
00:02:31,651 --> 00:02:34,362
I heard he threw his back out
climbing on his girlfriend.

48
00:02:34,528 --> 00:02:36,821
-Weather girl on Channel Two?
-That's the one.

49
00:02:36,989 --> 00:02:40,450
In any case,
they're asking me to fill in for him.

50
00:02:40,618 --> 00:02:43,329
In Switzerland
or with the big-boobed weather girl?

51
00:02:43,913 --> 00:02:47,124
Switzerland.
And I get to bring a guest.

52
00:02:47,291 --> 00:02:50,460
RAJESH: Oh, no way, dude!
-Oh, my God, this is incredible.

53
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:53,672
I'm so happy I'm not gonna question
their judgment in picking you.

54
00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:57,426
I'm just gonna run home
and start packing.

55
00:02:59,887 --> 00:03:02,097
Wait, why wouldn't you take Penny?

56
00:03:03,349 --> 00:03:05,768
I am taking Penny.

57
00:03:05,935 --> 00:03:07,770
Oh.

58
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:11,190
Then I anticipate an awkward situation
when you get home.

59
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:39,426
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

60
00:03:39,593 --> 00:03:43,680
-Sheldon, you got a minute?
-Of course, my good friend. Come in.

61
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:46,141
Yeah, help me out.

62
00:03:46,308 --> 00:03:50,395
Which ski hat says,
"Aprés Super Collider"?

63
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:54,400
Sheldon,
I'm not taking you to Switzerland.

64
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:57,278
Well, of course you are.
Who else would you take?

65
00:03:57,737 --> 00:04:00,322
-Penny.
“What? That's absurd.

66
00:04:00,489 --> 00:04:03,909
Penny has no interest
in subatomic particle research.

67
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:06,787
Yes, but it'll be Valentine's Day.

68
00:04:06,954 --> 00:04:11,083
We can go sightseeing and skiing
and make love in front of a roaring fire...

69
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:13,961
...In the shadow
of the snow-capped Alps.

70
00:04:15,588 --> 00:04:18,799
But Penny has no interest
in subatomic particle research.

71
00:04:19,633 --> 00:04:21,051
I'm sorry, Sheldon.

72
00:04:21,218 --> 00:04:25,096
Sorry? I've been dreaming about
going to the Large Hadron Collider...

73
00:04:25,264 --> 00:04:26,807
...since I was 9 years old.

74
00:04:26,974 --> 00:04:31,474
I've been dreaming about spending
Valentine's with a girl since I was 6.

75
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:34,064
Shame on you.

76
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:37,610
That's no dream for a scientist.

77
00:04:39,111 --> 00:04:42,489
-Okay, what's the big surprise?
-Just a minute.

78
00:04:43,115 --> 00:04:45,492
This tray contains clues...

79
00:04:45,659 --> 00:04:49,579
...as to what you and I are going
to be doing on Valentine's Day.

80
00:04:49,747 --> 00:04:52,708
Oh, wow, okay. Let's see.

81
00:04:52,875 --> 00:04:57,375
We've got milk chocolate,
Swiss cheese, fondue.

82
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:01,967
My lactose-intolerant boyfriend
is gonna eat all this...

83
00:05:02,134 --> 00:05:05,011
...then I'm gonna climb on his back
and rocket to the moon?

84
00:05:10,434 --> 00:05:12,102
No.

85
00:05:12,478 --> 00:05:14,605
But it does involve air travel.

86
00:05:16,315 --> 00:05:17,649
Okay. Um....

87
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:22,317
Let me slice this Swiss cheese
with my Swiss Army knife...

88
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,325
...and then you can wash it down...

89
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:30,496
...with a cup
of Swiss Miss instant cocoa.

90
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:33,624
Okay, I'm starting to think
"Swiss" is key here.

91
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:35,751
Uh-huh.

92
00:05:36,335 --> 00:05:39,379
We're going to Disneyland
and ride the Matterhorn.

93
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:43,175
How does that involve air travel?

94
00:05:44,677 --> 00:05:47,888
We're going to Disney World
and ride the Matterhorn.

95
00:05:48,931 --> 00:05:51,016
-No.
-Okay, sweetie, this started out fun...

96
00:05:51,183 --> 00:05:52,767
but I'm over it.

97
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:58,023
We're going to Switzerland
to see the CERN Super Collider.

98
00:06:00,776 --> 00:06:02,402
And ski. We'll also go skiing.

99
00:06:03,153 --> 00:06:05,989
-We're going skiing in Switzerland?
-You'll ski, I'll fall.

100
00:06:06,156 --> 00:06:10,118
But, yeah, we will be in Switzerland
for Valentine's Day.

101
00:06:10,286 --> 00:06:12,830
-Oh, my God, Leonard, that's incredible.
-Ha-ha-ha.

102
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:15,332
SHELDON:
Not so fast.

103
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:18,710
You might wanna hold off
on lighting your Raabeliechtli, Penny.

104
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:20,296
My ribee-what-ly?

105
00:06:20,754 --> 00:06:22,839
Raabeliechtli, it means turnip light...

106
00:06:23,007 --> 00:06:26,010
...and refers to a lantern
hand-carved from a root vegetable...

107
00:06:26,176 --> 00:06:29,345
...to celebrate Swiss festivals
which you'll not be celebrating...

108
00:06:29,513 --> 00:06:32,557
...because, A,
these festivals occur in the fall. ..

109
00:06:33,475 --> 00:06:36,686
...and B,
you will not be going to Switzerland.

110
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:39,857
Sheldon, we've been through this.
I'm taking Penny.

111
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:42,192
Afraid not. Do you recognize this?

112
00:06:42,359 --> 00:06:46,071
-Oh, not the roommate agreement.
-Indeed, the roommate agreement.

113
00:06:46,238 --> 00:06:48,907
I call your attention
to the Friendship Rider...

114
00:06:49,074 --> 00:06:51,534
...in Appendix C: Future Commitments.
Number 37:

115
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:55,872
"In the event one friend is ever invited
to visit the Large Hadron Collider...

116
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:59,960
...now under construction, he shall invite
the other friend to accompany him."

117
00:07:00,127 --> 00:07:01,545
Oh, for God's sakes.

118
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:04,548
You actually put that
in an agreement?

119
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:07,634
We put in what happens
if one of us wins a MacArthur Grant. ..

120
00:07:07,801 --> 00:07:12,301
...or if one of us gets superpowers,
or if one of us is bitten by a zombie.

121
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:15,642
He can't kill me. Even if I turn.

122
00:07:16,685 --> 00:07:19,437
Is there anything about
if one of you gets a girlfriend?

123
00:07:19,605 --> 00:07:21,898
No, that seemed a little far-fetched.

124
00:07:24,985 --> 00:07:27,696
Sheldon, do you really expect
to enforce this?

125
00:07:27,863 --> 00:07:30,448
I've lived up to my commitments
under the agreement.

126
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:34,411
At least once a day I ask how you are,
even though I simply don't care.

127
00:07:35,037 --> 00:07:38,957
I no longer stage spontaneous
bio hazard drills after 10 p.m.

128
00:07:39,124 --> 00:07:42,502
And I abandoned my goal
to master Tuvan throat singing.

129
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:44,755
- I shouldn't ask, but what is--7?
-No.

130
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:46,924
[VOCALIZING]

131
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:56,767
I'd be much further along
if I'd been allowed to practice.

132
00:07:57,393 --> 00:07:59,978
Look, Sheldon,
I know it's in the agreement.

133
00:08:00,145 --> 00:08:02,939
If you turn into a zombie,
I promise I will not Kill you.

134
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:07,277
In fact, I'll even let you eat my brains.
But I'm taking Penny to Switzerland.

135
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:09,780
-Is that your final decision??
-It is.

136
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:11,823
Very well.

137
00:08:14,576 --> 00:08:15,785
It's not over, is it?

138
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:17,912
What do you think?

139
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:20,665
[I SHELDON VOCALIZING]

140
00:08:31,635 --> 00:08:34,346
Got a bit of traffic this morning, huh?

141
00:08:38,308 --> 00:08:40,351
Think it's gonna rain?

142
00:08:42,187 --> 00:08:46,191
Instead of underpants, I covered
my crotch with potato salad. Thoughts?

143
00:08:48,652 --> 00:08:52,489
I know what'll cheer you up.
Let's play one of your driving games.

144
00:08:52,906 --> 00:08:56,492
All right. This game is called Traitors.

145
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:00,664
I will name three historical figures...

146
00:09:00,831 --> 00:09:03,708
...put them in order
of the heinousness of their betrayal:

147
00:09:03,876 --> 00:09:08,255
Benedict Arnold, Judas,
Dr. Leonard Hofstadter.

148
00:09:09,089 --> 00:09:11,800
You really think I belong
with Benedict Arnold and Judas?

149
00:09:12,176 --> 00:09:15,929
You're right. Judas had the decency
to hang himself after what he did.

150
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:20,851
Can't you at least try to understand
how much this means to me?

151
00:09:22,644 --> 00:09:27,144
Round two: Leonard Hofstadter,
Darth Vader, Rupert Murdoch.

152
00:09:27,816 --> 00:09:28,942
Rupert Murdoch?

153
00:09:29,234 --> 00:09:32,111
He owns Fox
and they cancelled Firefly.

154
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:37,826
Hint: He and Darth Vader
are tied for number two.

155
00:09:42,122 --> 00:09:45,125
Sorry, I couldn't hang with you.
I had a date with Bernadette.

156
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:48,253
I know. I saw the tweet.

157
00:09:48,545 --> 00:09:51,714
-So, what did you end up doing?
-Not much. Nuked a burrito. ..

158
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:54,467
...prayed to Hindu god Urvashi
your bowels'd loosen...

159
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:57,054
...and your penis would droop
like a willow tree.

160
00:09:58,847 --> 00:10:00,723
-You seen Sheldon?
-No.

161
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:04,644
-Is he still mad about the Super Collider?
-Yeah, he thinks I betrayed him.

162
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:06,980
What would you guys do
if you were me?

163
00:10:07,272 --> 00:10:09,399
I'd take Sheldon to Switzerland.

164
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:12,944
-Seriously?
-Absolutely. And I'd leave him there.

165
00:10:21,286 --> 00:10:23,079
What the hell is that?

166
00:10:23,247 --> 00:10:25,540
Uh, let's see.

167
00:10:25,707 --> 00:10:28,626
Yep, 30 pieces of silverware.

168
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:35,634
[RECORDER PLAYING]

169
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:37,803
[SIGHING]

170
00:10:50,732 --> 00:10:52,567
Morning, old chum.

171
00:10:52,734 --> 00:10:55,570
-What's going on?
-I've made you breakfast.

172
00:10:55,737 --> 00:10:57,572
Juice, coffee...

173
00:10:57,739 --> 00:11:01,617
...and pancakes in the shape of some
of your favorite fictional characters.

174
00:11:01,785 --> 00:11:03,745
See, here's Frodo.

175
00:11:03,912 --> 00:11:06,831
-You made Frodo pancakes?
-Yeah, I used coconut shavings...

176
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:08,959
to do the hair on his feet.

177
00:11:09,293 --> 00:11:11,962
If you need to void your bladder
before eating...

178
00:11:12,129 --> 00:11:15,590
...| can keep them warm with this beret
that I thoroughly laundered...

179
00:11:15,757 --> 00:11:18,593
...and pressed into service
as a pancake cozy.

180
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:21,096
Why are you doing this?

181
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:24,182
It's by way of an apology
for my recent behavior.

182
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:28,103
I've had some time to reflect
and I've come to realize. ..

183
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:31,273
...that friendship is not an aggregation
of written agreements.

184
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:35,777
It's the result of two people
respecting and caring for each other.

185
00:11:35,944 --> 00:11:40,198
-Butterscotch scone?
-Thanks.

186
00:11:41,617 --> 00:11:43,952
-It's good.
-What you're tasting is respect...

187
00:11:44,119 --> 00:11:45,411
and affection.

188
00:11:46,955 --> 00:11:48,998
And about a pound of Crisco.

189
00:11:50,125 --> 00:11:52,836
After breakfast,
I thought we could spend the day...

190
00:11:53,003 --> 00:11:56,631
...watching the final season of Babylon 5
with director commentary.

191
00:11:56,798 --> 00:11:58,299
You hate Babylon 5.

192
00:11:58,467 --> 00:12:02,679
I do. It fails as drama, science fiction
and it's hopelessly derivative.

193
00:12:02,846 --> 00:12:05,640
But you like it, and you're my friend.

194
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:07,809
Okay, great.

195
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:13,648
-Still not taking you to Switzerland.
-Drat.

196
00:12:17,527 --> 00:12:19,570
No Frodo for you.

197
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:25,661
SHELDON: Hello.
-Hello.

198
00:12:25,827 --> 00:12:27,870
Let's dispense
with the friendly banter.

199
00:12:29,331 --> 00:12:30,749
I believe you know why I'm here.

200
00:12:31,166 --> 00:12:33,334
Well, I always figured
it was to study us...

201
00:12:33,502 --> 00:12:37,380
...discover our weaknesses,
and report back to your alien overlords.

202
00:12:38,507 --> 00:12:40,509
Yes, amusing.

203
00:12:40,676 --> 00:12:44,179
Extraordinary intelligence might well
appear extraterrestrial to you...

204
00:12:44,346 --> 00:12:46,514
...but let me be more specific.

205
00:12:46,682 --> 00:12:49,726
I believe you know why I'm here
in the laundry room.

206
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:52,395
Better acoustics
for your throat singing?

207
00:12:54,022 --> 00:12:56,691
[VOCALIZING]

208
00:13:00,529 --> 00:13:02,030
It's actually not bad.

209
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:07,536
But my true purpose in being here
will be revealed. ..

210
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:11,790
...In this brief PowerPoint presentation.
Ahem. Lights.

211
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:22,718
"Why Sheldon Cooper, PhD...

212
00:13:22,884 --> 00:13:25,261
...should go to Switzerland
to see the CERN Super Collider:

213
00:13:25,429 --> 00:13:27,806
A PowerPoint presentation
by Sheldon Cooper, PhD."

214
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:30,767
Oh, for God's sakes.

215
00:13:31,768 --> 00:13:35,980
Here, we have a highly gifted researcher
in the field of particle physics...

216
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:37,941
...whose work has brought him
to the precipice...

217
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:42,153
...of forever changing mankind's
understanding of the universe, a.k.a. me.

218
00:13:43,655 --> 00:13:47,575
And here, we have a waitress
brushing her teeth with her finger.

219
00:13:48,910 --> 00:13:50,786
A.k.a. you.

220
00:13:51,246 --> 00:13:53,456
Sorry.
Is this supposed to be buttering me up?

221
00:13:53,623 --> 00:13:56,584
Please hold all questions
until the end of the presentation.

222
00:13:56,752 --> 00:14:00,464
This is the Large Hadron Collider
at CERN in Switzerland.

223
00:14:00,630 --> 00:14:03,591
The product of decades
of planning and construction.

224
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:06,470
It is a mecca
for physicists the world over.

225
00:14:07,095 --> 00:14:11,099
This is Bath and Body Works
on Colorado Boulevard.

226
00:14:11,266 --> 00:14:15,103
They sell scented soaps and lotions.
Some of which contain glitter.

227
00:14:15,270 --> 00:14:18,439
Now, let's see
if we can match the individual. ..

228
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:20,442
...to the appropriate destination.

229
00:14:20,984 --> 00:14:22,986
Okay. Show's over.

230
00:14:23,153 --> 00:14:25,613
No, it's not. I've got five more slides.

231
00:14:26,156 --> 00:14:27,949
Sheldon, this is Leonard's decision.

232
00:14:28,116 --> 00:14:30,493
He invited me to Switzerland
and I intend to go.

233
00:14:34,456 --> 00:14:36,124
Very well.

234
00:14:36,875 --> 00:14:38,793
Enjoy yourself.

235
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:42,463
You're gonna be in the presence of
something I've dreamed of for decades.

236
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:45,383
I hope you'll appreciate...

237
00:14:45,592 --> 00:14:48,636
...the magnitude of where you are,
and what it represents.

238
00:14:51,807 --> 00:14:53,183
I'll talk to Leonard.

239
00:14:54,893 --> 00:14:57,061
-You will?
Yes.

240
00:14:57,229 --> 00:14:59,981
If it means that much to you,
you should go.

241
00:15:00,482 --> 00:15:03,693
Oh, Penny, thank you.

242
00:15:05,487 --> 00:15:07,989
-You're welcome.
-Since I rarely hug...

243
00:15:08,156 --> 00:15:11,367
...I'm relying on your expertise
regarding duration.

244
00:15:12,202 --> 00:15:14,621
- I think we're there.
-Oh, good.

245
00:15:15,622 --> 00:15:16,706
Bye-bye.

246
00:15:21,044 --> 00:15:25,339
Even though I don't have a girlfriend, I
can still have a good time on Valentine's.

247
00:15:25,507 --> 00:15:27,884
Trust me, you can't. I've tried.

248
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:30,762
No, no, no.
I'm gonna have a "me" day.

249
00:15:30,929 --> 00:15:33,514
I'm gonna go
to one of those spas in Koreatown...

250
00:15:33,682 --> 00:15:35,225
...take a steam, get a massage.

251
00:15:35,392 --> 00:15:39,396
Then I'm gonna stop at a pet store
and get licked by puppies.

252
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:45,276
-Sheldon, I need to talk to you.
-All right, my friend.

253
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:46,903
Would you like some cholermus?

254
00:15:47,195 --> 00:15:48,738
-Some what?
-Cholermus.

255
00:15:48,905 --> 00:15:50,865
It's a traditional Swiss breakfast dish.

256
00:15:51,032 --> 00:15:55,244
I'm preparing my gastrointestinal system
for the exotic cuisine of Switzerland.

257
00:15:56,163 --> 00:15:59,875
-You're not going to Switzerland.
-Oh, but I am.

258
00:16:00,041 --> 00:16:01,917
Didn't Penny tell you the good news?

259
00:16:02,085 --> 00:16:05,630
You went behind my back to guilt her
into letting you go instead of her.

260
00:16:05,797 --> 00:16:07,882
Yes, that good news.

261
00:16:09,092 --> 00:16:12,303
Forget it. I was the one invited,
I get to decide who goes with me.

262
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:14,055
And it's Penny, not you.

263
00:16:14,431 --> 00:16:18,101
Howard, could you lower the lights?
I have a short PowerPoint presentation.

264
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:22,146
I don't need to see your presentation.
This discussion is over.

265
00:16:22,314 --> 00:16:25,775
Well, that's a somewhat
ambiguous response. Am I going or not?

266
00:16:26,318 --> 00:16:27,902
Sheldon, at this point...

267
00:16:28,069 --> 00:16:30,571
... would go by myself
before I would take you.

268
00:16:30,739 --> 00:16:32,949
-Really?
-Yeah, really.

269
00:16:33,325 --> 00:16:36,244
Well, then.
You leave me no alternative.

270
00:16:36,411 --> 00:16:39,080
From this moment forward,
we can be roommates. ..

271
00:16:39,247 --> 00:16:40,998
...but we will no longer be friends.

272
00:16:41,458 --> 00:16:43,084
I'm sorry you feel that way.

273
00:16:43,251 --> 00:16:45,920
I don't think you're fully aware
of the ramifications here, Leonard.

274
00:16:46,087 --> 00:16:47,421
[LEONARD SIGHS]

275
00:16:47,589 --> 00:16:49,465
Why don't you enlighten me?

276
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:52,344
With the friendship clause
of our agreement nullified...

277
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:54,804
...you're no longer entitled
to accompany me to go swimming...

278
00:16:54,971 --> 00:16:56,847
...at Bill Gates' house
should I be invited.

279
00:17:02,354 --> 00:17:03,980
Ooh, that's gotta sting.

280
00:17:07,984 --> 00:17:10,945
Think, this time tomorrow,
we'll be in Geneva, Switzerland...

281
00:17:11,112 --> 00:17:14,281
-...for our first Valentine's Day.
- I know.

282
00:17:14,449 --> 00:17:18,453
I went shopping today and bought
special undies for the occasion.

283
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:21,122
Thermal? Because it's gonna be cold.

284
00:17:21,289 --> 00:17:23,541
Think it through, Leonard.

285
00:17:24,292 --> 00:17:25,626
-Oh.
-Oh.

286
00:17:25,794 --> 00:17:27,670
[BOTH LAUGH]

287
00:17:27,837 --> 00:17:29,046
[SNEEZING]

288
00:17:29,214 --> 00:17:30,632
Gesundheit.

289
00:17:30,799 --> 00:17:34,260
Or as they say in Switzerland,
gesundheit.

290
00:17:35,887 --> 00:17:40,141
-Getting a cold?
-No, no, it's probably just allergies.

291
00:17:41,518 --> 00:17:43,686
You want an allergy pill?
I have them all.

292
00:17:43,853 --> 00:17:47,481
Prescription, nonprescription, foreign,
domestic, experimental.

293
00:17:47,857 --> 00:17:49,233
Do any of them work?

294
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:52,529
Not really, I'm just an enthusiast.

295
00:17:53,613 --> 00:17:55,323
[BLOWS NOSE]

296
00:17:57,701 --> 00:18:00,620
[PENNY RETCHES]

297
00:18:02,914 --> 00:18:03,956
Penny?

298
00:18:04,124 --> 00:18:05,875
[TOILET FLUSHES]

299
00:18:06,042 --> 00:18:07,334
You okay?

300
00:18:07,502 --> 00:18:10,421
PENNY:
Did that sound okay to you?

301
00:18:11,339 --> 00:18:13,841
Do not come in here.

302
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:15,510
What's going on?

303
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:18,596
PENNY: I'm having a tea party.
What do you think is going on?

304
00:18:18,763 --> 00:18:20,890
[PENNY HAWKS AND SPITS]

305
00:18:21,808 --> 00:18:24,060
I think I might have the flu.

306
00:18:24,227 --> 00:18:26,437
[PENNY VOMITS]

307
00:18:26,605 --> 00:18:28,231
Or the plague.

308
00:18:30,692 --> 00:18:34,529
Well, our plane leaves at 9 a.m.
Do you think you'll feel better by then?

309
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:36,948
[PENNY VOMITS]

310
00:18:37,115 --> 00:18:40,326
PENNY:
Yep. Because I'm gonna be dead.

311
00:18:43,538 --> 00:18:45,456
Hey, Sheldon?

312
00:18:45,707 --> 00:18:49,293
Listen, Penny's sick and she's not
gonna be able to go to Switzerland...

313
00:18:49,461 --> 00:18:53,590
...So if you're still interested,
you're welcome to come.

314
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:56,426
[VOMITING THEN COUGHING]

315
00:18:57,719 --> 00:18:59,387
[TOILET FLUSHES]

316
00:19:01,556 --> 00:19:03,766
Great. I'll start packing.

317
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:07,604
In 2 minute.

318
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:11,357
[SHELDON VOMITING]

319
00:19:11,775 --> 00:19:14,903
Oh, look, it's the cholermus.

320
00:19:21,242 --> 00:19:23,911
[COUGHING THEN BLOWS NOSE]

321
00:19:25,538 --> 00:19:28,207
Ugh. Here's your soup.

322
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:29,834
-Chicken?
Yes.

323
00:19:30,001 --> 00:19:31,752
-With the little stars?
Yes.

324
00:19:31,961 --> 00:19:33,379
Heated to 180 degrees?

325
00:19:34,464 --> 00:19:37,425
Why don't I pour it in your lap
and you can tell me?

326
00:19:38,385 --> 00:19:41,096
You don't have to be mean. I'm sick.

327
00:19:41,262 --> 00:19:45,057
-Yeah, well, I'm sick too.
-Not my problem.

328
00:19:46,476 --> 00:19:48,561
I don't understand
how this happened to me.

329
00:19:48,895 --> 00:19:52,940
I'm scrupulous about my hygiene,
I regularly disinfect my hands...

330
00:19:53,108 --> 00:19:57,237
...and I avoid contact with other people
on general principle.

331
00:19:57,612 --> 00:19:59,614
I don't know what to tell you,
Sheldon.

332
00:20:02,283 --> 00:20:05,035
SHELDON:
Oh, Penny, thank you.

333
00:20:05,995 --> 00:20:07,997
You're welcome.

334
00:20:14,045 --> 00:20:17,548
It's you. I touched you.

335
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:20,134
Happy Valentine's Day.

336
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:32,897
Oh, my goodness, look at this room.

337
00:20:33,064 --> 00:20:34,106
[GASPS]

338
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:38,774
Champagne, roses,
oh, and little chocolates.

339
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:43,283
This is going to be
the best Valentine's Day ever.

340
00:20:44,576 --> 00:20:47,495
Yeah, I forgot about all this.

341
00:20:47,954 --> 00:20:49,497
But I never will.

342
00:21:18,902 --> 00:21:20,904
[ENGLISH - US - SDH]

